# Project persistence intermediates
# A staging sibling exists only between a write and its atomic replacement; one left
# behind by an interrupted save holds project content and is never published.
*.rino-staging
# Package export writes a private sibling until archive verification and atomic replacement finish.
*.rino-package.rino-staging-*
# Native Pipeline import sessions are private application-cache staging and may contain
# source-derived project data while a transaction is in flight.
*.rino-import-staging
# Signed packages prepared for an explicit GitHub upload are short-lived private cache.
**/publishing-cache/
# Synced Rino_WFP templates and injected application bundles contain local build metadata
# and unpublished user projects; they never belong to the authoring repository.
/_WFP/
**/wfp-template-cache/
*.rino-app.zip.rino-staging-*
*.rino-app.zip

